<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marquis Wen of Wei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 445–396 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Marquess Wen of Wei, Wei Si</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marquis Wen of Wei was the founding ruler of the state of Wei, recognised as a state by the Zhou king in 403 BCE after the partition of Jin. He made Wei the leading power of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a> through the legal reforms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-kui">Li Kui</a>, the irrigation works of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ximen-bao">Ximen Bao</a> and the professional army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-qi">Wu Qi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marquis-wen-of-wei.jpg" alt="Marquis Wen of Wei" width="250" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown Uploaded by Philg88 at en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WeiWenHou%E9%AD%8F%E6%96%87%E4%BE%AF.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
